{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>My righteousness is drawn near.</b> To bring it, and this is the reason for בא:" "<b>It shall not tarry.</b> It takes מבוא with it, by way of illustration, because it is a transitive verb [lit. an exiting verb]." "<b>And I will give.</b> It draws after it עמו, and likewise: ונתתי לישראל תפארתי. Or its meaning is: לישראל, for they are תפארתי, and this is the correct interpretation, like אשר בך אתפאר (Isaiah 49:3)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {2 "The phrase ונתתי לישראל תפארתי appears to be a partial quotation of the continuation of Isaiah 46:13 rather than a separate verse citation; translated as retained Hebrew since it functions as part of his grammatical argument."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:23.079088341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}